summary:
  A text colour is handed back as it came, whether it can be read or not.

history:
  On Breeze Light the playing station's name was a bright green on its
  row's pale green wash, 1.23:1 where body text wants 4.5:1. The text
  colours are measured against the popup and the wash and walked toward
  black or white until they read; this makes every colour pass the
  measurement.

target:
  package/contents/ui/ColorLogic.js

find:
      if (worstContrast(fg, bg, wash) >= want) return fg;

replace:
      if (worstContrast(fg, bg, wash) >= 0) return fg;

expect:
  Killed by tst_colorlogic::test_a_light_scheme_gets_a_green_it_can_read.
  Line-neutral.
